            "transcript": "China has taken major strides in both satellite-based computing and reusable rocket technology in 2026. In March, the country successfully launched the Tiansuan-1 space computing experimental satellite, officially kicking off the Space Computing Constellation program. The constellation is planned to consist of over 100 low-orbit satellites forming a space-based computing network that provides real-time computational services to ground users. According to the Zhejiang Laboratory, which leads the project, the constellation has already demonstrated four core capabilities after nine months of in-orbit testing: networking, on-board computing, model deployment, and scientific payload verification. The single-satellite maximum computing power reaches 744 TOPS, making it the world's largest orbital computing constellation.\n\nIn May, China Aerospace Science and Technology Corporation achieved another milestone: the first successful sea-based recovery test of the Long March 10 launch vehicle. After completing its launch mission, the rocket's first- stage booster precisely landed on an unmanned recovery vessel stationed in a designated area of the South China Sea. This breakthrough in reusable rocket technology makes China the second country after the United States to master large-scale rocket sea recovery.\n\nFurthermore, in June 2026, the Tianwen-3 Mars sample return mission received formal approval. The mission, scheduled for launch in 2028, aims to retrieve soil and rock samples from the Martian surface and return them to Earth for analysis — a feat no other nation has yet accomplished.\n\nQuestion 12: What is the purpose of the \"Space Computing Constellation\"?\nQuestion 13: Where did the Long March 10 rocket's first stage land during its recovery test?\nQuestion 14: What was approved in June 2026, according to the passage?",
            "translation": "2026年，中国在卫星计算和可重复使用火箭技术两方面都迈出了重大步伐。3月，中国成功发射“天算一号”太空计算实验卫星，正式启动太空计算星座计划。该星座计划由100多颗低轨道卫星组成，构成一个向地面用户提供实时计算服务的天基计算网络。据牵头该项目的之江实验室介绍，经过九个月的在轨测试，该星座已展示出四项核心能力：组网、星上计算、模型部署和科学载荷验证。单颗卫星的最大算力达到744 TOPS，使其成为全球规模最大的在轨计算星座。\n\n5月，中国航天科技集团实现了又一座里程碑：“长征十号”运载火箭首次海上回收试验成功。完成发射任务后，火箭一级助推器精准降落在部署于南海指定海域的一艘无人回收船上。这一可重复使用火箭技术的突破，使中国成为继美国之后第二个掌握大规模火箭海上回收技术的国家。\n\n此外，2026年6月，“天问三号”火星采样返回任务正式获批。该任务计划于2028年发射，旨在从火星表面采集土壤和岩石样本并带回地球进行分析——这是迄今还没有任何其他国家完成的壮举。\n\nQuestion 12: “太空计算星座”的用途是什么？\nQuestion 13: 在回收试验中，“长征十号”火箭的一级落在了哪里？\nQuestion 14: 根据短文，2026年6月获批的是什么？"
