            "transcript": "The 2026 CCTV 3·15 Gala, broadcast on March 15, once again sent shockwaves through China's consumer market by exposing a series of egregious violations of consumer rights, with food safety taking center stage.\n\nThe most alarming investigation revealed a network of workshops in central China that had been reprocessing expired frozen meat products—some dating back to 2022—by washing them with chemical solutions, re-seasoning them heavily, and repackaging them with falsified production dates for sale at discount supermarkets and food delivery platforms. Investigators traced the operation across three provinces, involving at least 12 processing sites that had collectively distributed over 500 tons of potentially hazardous food products.\n\nThe broadcast also uncovered fraud in the premium cooking oil industry, where certain manufacturers were blending low-grade rapeseed oil with industrial-grade oil and marketing it as \"first-press extra virgin\" cooking oil. Laboratory tests commissioned by the program found that samples contained carcinogenic compounds at levels exceeding national safety standards by up to 40 times.\n\nIn the weeks following the broadcast, the State Administration for Market Regulation launched a nationwide inspection campaign covering over 8,000 food processing facilities. By April 2026, 47 arrests had been made, 23 production licenses were revoked, and fines totaling 380 million yuan were imposed. The government also announced a mandatory blockchain-based food traceability system for all processed meat and edible oil products, scheduled to take effect in January 2027.\n\nQuestion 12: What was the most shocking revelation in the 2026 3·15 Gala?\nQuestion 13: How many processing sites were involved in the expired meat scandal?\nQuestion 14: What long-term regulatory measure did the government announce after the broadcast?",
            "translation": "2026年央视3·15晚会于3月15日播出，再次震动中国消费市场，曝光了一系列严重侵害消费者权益的违法行为，其中食品安全成为焦点。\n\n最令人震惊的调查揭露了华中地区的一批作坊网络，它们把过期的冷冻肉制品——有的甚至可追溯到2022年——用化学溶液清洗、大量重新调味，并篡改生产日期后重新包装，销往折扣超市和外卖平台。调查人员追踪到该团伙跨三个省份经营，至少涉及12处加工点，累计分销了500多吨存在潜在危害的食品。\n\n晚会还揭开了高端食用油行业的造假黑幕：某些生产商把低等级菜籽油与工业用油勾兑，却标榜为“头道初榨”食用油对外销售。节目委托的实验室检测发现，样品中的致癌物含量超出国家安全标准最高达40倍。\n\n晚会播出后的几周内，国家市场监督管理总局启动了覆盖8000多家食品加工企业的全国性检查行动。截至2026年4月，已有47人被逮捕，23张生产许可证被吊销，罚款总额达3.8亿元。政府还宣布对全部加工肉制品和食用油产品实行基于区块链的强制性食品追溯体系，该体系定于2027年1月生效。\n\nQuestion 12: 2026年3·15晚会中最令人震惊的揭露是什么？\nQuestion 13: 过期肉丑闻涉及多少处加工点？\nQuestion 14: 晚会播出后政府宣布了什么长期监管措施？"
