            "transcript": "The summer of 2026 witnessed an unprecedented surge in green consumption across China, signaling a fundamental shift in consumer behavior that experts believe may be permanent rather than seasonal.\n\nData from multiple e-commerce platforms showed that during the June-to-August period, sales of products certified with the \"China Green Product\" label increased by 67% year-on-year, while searches for \"sustainable,\" \"biodegradable,\" and \"carbon-neutral\" products rose by 214%. Particularly notable was the explosive growth in the refurbished electronics market, which expanded by 89% as younger consumers increasingly embraced the concept of extending product lifecycles rather than chasing the newest models.\n\nA survey conducted by the China Consumers Association in August 2026, covering 12,000 respondents across 30 cities, found that 64% of consumers aged 18–35 said they were willing to pay a premium of 10%–25% for environmentally sustainable products, up from 41% in a similar 2024 survey. The top three categories for green spending were personal care products (biodegradable packaging), fashion (recycled materials), and home appliances (energy efficiency class A+++).\n\nIndustry analysts attribute this shift to multiple converging factors: the continued impact of the government's \"dual carbon\" goals, increased media coverage of climate-related extreme weather events throughout 2025–2026, and a growing number of brands that have successfully made sustainability a core part of their identity rather than a marketing afterthought. However, experts also caution that \"greenwashing\"—where companies make misleading claims about environmental benefits—remains a significant challenge, calling for stricter certification standards and consumer education. compared to the previous year? for sustainable products in 2026?\n\nQuestion 15: By what percentage did sales of \"China Green Product\" labeled goods increase in summer 2026\nQuestion 16: According to the consumer survey, what proportion of young consumers said they would pay extra\nQuestion 17: What concern do experts raise about the green consumption trend?",
            "translation": "2026年夏天，中国见证了前所未有的绿色消费激增，标志着消费者行为发生了根本性转变，专家认为这种转变可能是长期性的，而非季节性的。\n\n多个电商平台的数据显示，在6月至8月期间，带有“中国绿色产品”认证标志的产品销售额同比增长67%，而对“可持续”“可生物降解”和“碳中和”产品的搜索量上升了214%。尤其引人注目的是翻新电子产品市场的爆发式增长，其规模扩大了89%，因为年轻消费者越来越接受延长产品生命周期、而不是追逐最新型号的理念。\n\n中国消费者协会2026年8月开展的一项覆盖30个城市、12000名受访者的调查发现，18至35岁的消费者中有64%表示愿意为环保可持续产品多支付10%至25%的溢价，而2024年同类调查中这一比例仅为41%。绿色消费的前三大品类是个人护理用品（可生物降解包装）、时尚服饰（再生材料）和家用电器（A+++能效等级）。\n\n行业分析师将这一转变归因于多个因素的叠加：政府“双碳”目标的持续影响、2025至2026年间媒体对气候相关极端天气事件报道的增加，以及越来越多品牌成功地将可持续性打造成自身核心身份、而非营销上的事后补充。不过，专家也提醒，“漂绿”——即企业对环保效益作误导性宣称——仍是一项重大挑战，需要更严格的认证标准和消费者教育。\n\nQuestion 15: 2026年夏天“中国绿色产品”标志商品的销售额与上年同期相比增长了百分之多少？\nQuestion 16: 根据消费者调查，有多少比例的年轻消费者表示愿意在2026年为可持续产品支付额外费用？\nQuestion 17: 专家对绿色消费趋势提出了什么担忧？"
