    "writing": {
      "topic": "Live-streaming shopping has become increasingly popular in China, with billions of yuan in sales generated through platforms like Douyin, Kuaishou, and Taobao Live. However, this new form of commerce has also given rise to widespread problems, including false advertising, exaggerated product claims, and misleading marketing tactics that exploit consumer trust. Discuss the measures that should be taken—by government regulators, e-commerce platforms, and consumers themselves—to protect consumers in the context of live-streaming shopping.",
      "outline": "1. Identify the key problems associated with live-streaming shopping.\n2. Propose specific measures that different stakeholders should take.\n3. Conclude with your assessment of how these measures can create a healthier live-streaming commerce environment.\nWrite at least 150 words.",
      "sampleEssay": "Towards a Safer Live-Streaming Shopping Environment\n\nLive-streaming shopping, while revolutionary, is plagued by significant problems. False advertising and exaggerated product claims are rampant, as hosts often prioritize sales over truth. This erodes consumer trust and leads to financial losses.\n\nTo address these issues, a multi-stakeholder approach is essential. Government regulators should enforce stricter penalties for fraudulent claims and mandate transparent disclosure of all sponsorship deals. E-commerce platforms must take responsibility by implementing robust pre-screening mechanisms for live content and establishing clear, easily accessible channels for consumer complaints and refunds. Consumers themselves need to cultivate a critical mindset, verifying product claims with official certifications and exercising caution with “limited-time” offers.\n\nIn conclusion, through a combination of stricter regulation, platform accountability, and informed consumer behavior, the live-streaming marketplace can be transformed into a healthier environment where innovation and consumer protection go hand in hand.",
      "sampleEssayZh": "迈向更安全的直播购物环境\n\n直播购物虽然具有革命性，却也深受诸多严重问题的困扰。虚假广告和夸大其词的产品宣传十分泛滥，因为主播们往往把销量置于真相之上。这侵蚀了消费者的信任，并导致经济损失。\n\n要解决这些问题，多方共同参与的方式至关重要。政府监管部门应对虚假宣传实施更严厉的处罚，并要求对所有赞助合作进行透明披露。电商平台必须承担责任，建立完善的直播内容预审机制，并设立清晰、便捷的消费者投诉与退款渠道。消费者自身也需要培养批判性思维，用官方认证来核实产品宣传，并对“限时”优惠保持警惕。\n\n总之，通过更严格的监管、平台的责任担当以及理性的消费行为三者相结合，直播购物市场可以转变为一个更健康的环境，让创新与消费者保护携手并进。"
    }
