            "transcript": "The year 2026 has delivered an extraordinary series of extreme weather events that scientists say bear the unmistakable fingerprint of a warming climate. In the United Kingdom, the village of Coningsby in Lincolnshire recorded a stunning 35.1°C on May 19 — the highest May temperature ever observed in British history, shattering the previous record of 32.8°C set in 1922. The Met Office issued its first-ever \"extreme heat\" warning for the month of May, and the National Health Service reported a 42% spike in heat-related emergency admissions compared to the May average. Public cooling centers were opened across London, Birmingham, and Manchester, a measure usually reserved for mid-summer.\n\nMeanwhile, in South Asia, the situation was far more dire. The Indian Meteorological Department confirmed that the town of Phalodi in Rajasthan reached 48.2°C on June 3, while the national capital region of Delhi experienced 16 consecutive days above 44°C — the longest such stretch on record. The heatwave claimed over 1,400 lives across India and Pakistan, with outdoor workers, the elderly, and residents of informal settlements bearing the heaviest toll. Hospitals in affected regions reported being overwhelmed by cases of heatstroke and severe dehydration.\n\nOn the other side of the globe, the United States was not spared. A \"heat dome\" settled over the Southwest in July, pushing temperatures in Phoenix, Arizona to 47.8°C for five straight days. Simultaneously, the Mississippi River basin experienced what meteorologists called a \"flash drought\" — rainfall deficits of over 60% in some areas over just six weeks — disrupting barge traffic and threatening the autumn harvest.\n\nQuestion 9: What record did the UK break in May 2026?\nQuestion 10: How many consecutive days above 44°C did Delhi experience in 2026?\nQuestion 11: What weather phenomenon affected the Mississippi River basin in July 2026?",
            "translation": "2026年出现了一系列极端天气事件，科学家称这些事件带有气候变暖的鲜明印记。在英国，林肯郡的科宁斯比村于5月19日录得惊人的35.1℃高温，这是英国有史以来5月的最高气温，打破了1922年创下的32.8℃纪录。英国气象局首次发布了5月份的“极端高温”预警，国家医疗服务体系报告称，与5月平均水平相比，高温相关急诊入院人数激增了42%。伦敦、伯明翰和曼彻斯特都开设了公共避暑中心，而这种措施通常只有盛夏才会采用。\n\n与此同时，南亚的情况要严峻得多。印度气象局证实，拉贾斯坦邦的帕洛迪镇6月3日气温达到48.2℃，而首都德里地区经历了连续16天超过44℃的高温——这是有记录以来持续时间最长的一次。这场热浪在印度和巴基斯坦夺走了1400多条生命，户外劳动者、老年人和非正规聚居区的居民承受的损失最为惨重。受灾地区的医院报告称，中暑和严重脱水的病例令医院不堪重负。\n\n在地球的另一端，美国也未能幸免。7月，一股“热穹顶”笼罩美国西南部，将亚利桑那州凤凰城的气温连续五天推高到47.8℃。与此同时，密西西比河流域经历了气象学家所称的“骤旱”——部分地区在短短六周内降雨量亏缺超过60%——这扰乱了驳船运输，并威胁到秋收。\n\nQuestion 9: 2026年5月英国打破了什么纪录？\nQuestion 10: 2026年德里经历了多少天超过44℃的高温？\nQuestion 11: 2026年7月影响密西西比河流域的是什么天气现象？"
