            "explanation": "细节理解题。问题问：与2025年同期相比，2026年上半年中国的碳强度下降了 百分之多少？根据原文 “China's carbon intensity... declined by 5.2% in the first half of 2026 compared to the same period in 2025” (与2025年同期相比，2026年上半年中国的碳强度下降了5.2%)，可知B项正确。",
            "transcript": "China's pursuit of its \"dual carbon\" goals — peaking carbon dioxide emissions before 2030 and achieving carbon neutrality by 2060 — reached several significant milestones in 2026, reflecting both policy momentum and structural economic transformation.\n\nAccording to data released by the National Bureau of Statistics in July 2026, China's carbon intensity — the amount of CO₂ emitted per unit of GDP — declined by 5.2% in the first half of 2026 compared to the same period in 2025, the largest half-year reduction since the dual carbon targets were announced in 2020. This acceleration was driven primarily by the rapid expansion of renewable energy capacity: in the first six months of 2026, China installed 98 gigawatts of new solar and wind capacity, accounting for 67% of all new electricity generation capacity added during the period. Total installed renewable capacity surpassed 1,800 gigawatts in June, placing China firmly on track to meet its 2030 target of 1,200 gigawatts of wind and solar capacity — six years ahead of schedule.\n\nThe annual National Energy Conservation Week, held from June 13 to 19, 2026, took on particular significance against this backdrop. Organized under the theme \"Green Transition, Shared Future,\" the campaign featured nationwide initiatives including energy-saving technology exhibitions in 36 major cities, a \"Low-Carbon Campus\" program involving over 500 universities, and the launch of the \"Carbon Inclusion\" platform — a digital system that allows individual citizens to earn points for low-carbon behaviors such as using public transportation, recycling, and reducing plastic consumption. These points can be redeemed for public service discounts, creating what policymakers describe as a \"positive incentive loop\" for individual climate action.\n\nSpeaking at the opening ceremony, the Minister of Ecology and Environment noted that China's carbon market — the world's largest by covered emissions — had expanded in 2026 to include the building materials and non- ferrous metals sectors, bringing the total share of national emissions covered by carbon pricing to over 70%. Carbon allowance prices on the national Emissions Trading System reached 105 yuan per ton in August 2026, up from 56 yuan at the start of 2024, signaling growing market confidence in the durability of China's climate policy framework. period in 2025?\n\nQuestion 15: By how much did China's carbon intensity decline in the first half of 2026 compared to the same\nQuestion 16: What was the theme of the 2026 National Energy Conservation Week?\nQuestion 17: According to the passage, what new development occurred in China's carbon market in 2026?",
            "translation": "中国对“双碳”目标的追求——在2030年前实现二氧化碳排放达峰、到2060年实现碳中和——在2026年取得了若干重要里程碑，这既反映了政策力度，也反映了经济结构转型。\n\n根据国家统计局2026年7月发布的数据，2026年上半年中国的碳强度——即单位GDP排放的二氧化碳量——与2025年同期相比下降了5.2%，这是自2020年宣布双碳目标以来最大的半年降幅。这一加速主要得益于可再生能源装机容量的快速扩张：2026年前六个月，中国新增太阳能和风电装机9800万千瓦，占同期全部新增发电装机的67%。6月，可再生能源总装机突破18亿千瓦，使中国稳稳走在提前六年实现2030年风电、太阳能装机12亿千瓦目标的轨道上。\n\n在此背景下，于2026年6月13日至19日举行的年度全国节能宣传周具有了特殊意义。本届宣传周以“绿色转型，共享未来”为主题，在全国范围内开展了一系列活动，包括在36个主要城市举办节能技术展览、覆盖500多所高校的“低碳校园”项目，以及推出“碳普惠”平台——一个让个人公民通过乘坐公共交通、回收利用和减少塑料消费等低碳行为获得积分的数字系统。这些积分可以兑换公共服务优惠，从而形成政策制定者所称的个人气候行动的“正向激励循环”。\n\n生态环境部部长在开幕式上致辞时指出，中国碳市场——按覆盖排放量计算是全球最大的碳市场——已于2026年扩大，将建材和有色金属行业纳入其中，使全国排放被碳定价覆盖的总体比例超过70%。全国碳排放权交易市场的碳配额价格在2026年8月达到每吨105元，而2024年初仅为56元，这表明市场对中国气候政策框架的持久性信心日益增强。\n\nQuestion 15: 与2025年同期相比，2026年上半年中国的碳强度下降了多少？\nQuestion 16: 2026年全国节能宣传周的主题是什么？\nQuestion 17: 根据短文，2026年中国碳市场出现了什么新进展？"
