            "answer": "B",
            "explanation": "细节理解题。问题问：根据2026年健康倡议，城市地区社区心理健康服务站的 目标是什么？根据原文 “the target is one community mental health station for every 50,000 residents” (目标是 每5万名居民设一个社区心理健康服务站)，可知B项“每5万名居民有一个服务站”正确。",
            "transcript": "In January 2026, the National Health Commission unveiled its annual \"Ten Practical Health Services for the People,\" a comprehensive package backed by 47 billion yuan in central government funding. The initiative represents one of the most ambitious expansions of public health services in China's recent history, with mental health access, preventive care, and women's health as its three flagship priorities.\n\nThe mental health component is arguably the most transformative. By the end of 2026, every county-level hospital in China is required to establish a dedicated psychological counseling outpatient clinic staffed by at least one full-time licensed professional. In urban areas, the target is one community mental health station for every 50,000 residents. To overcome the severe shortage of qualified personnel — China currently graduates only about 5,000 clinical psychology students per year — the government launched an accelerated training program aiming to produce 30,000 additional mental health workers over a three-year period through university expansion, online certification, and retraining of existing medical staff.\n\nWeight management constitutes the second major pillar. Recognizing that obesity and overweight now affect more than 50% of Chinese adults — a figure that has nearly doubled since 2000 — the initiative mandates free nutrition counseling, physical activity prescriptions, and BMI screening at all community health centers. A notable feature is the integration of weight management with mental health services, reflecting growing evidence that obesity and depression are bidirectional risk factors: each increases the likelihood of the other, and treating one without addressing the other often yields poor results.\n\nWomen's health received particular attention. The HPV vaccination program, previously limited to girls aged 13–15 in select cities, was expanded nationwide to cover all girls and young women aged 9–26, with free doses provided. Additionally, 15 pilot cities began offering free HPV vaccination to boys and young men in the same age range, acknowledging the role of gender-neutral vaccination in achieving herd immunity against cervical cancer and other HPV-related diseases. By June 2026, over 18 million doses had been administered under the expanded program.\n\nCancer screening was also significantly expanded. Building on successful pilot programs, free screening for",
            "translation": "2026年1月，国家卫健委公布了年度\"民生健康十件实事\"，这是一套由中央政府470亿元资金支持的综合性方案。该行动是中国近年来公共卫生服务最雄心勃勃的扩展之一，以心理健康可及性、预防保健和妇女健康作为三大重点优先事项。\n\n心理健康部分可以说是最具变革性的。到2026年底，中国每家县级医院都必须设立专门的心理咨询门诊，并配备至少一名全职持证专业人员。在城市地区，目标是每5万名居民设一个社区心理健康服务站。为克服合格人才严重短缺的问题——中国目前每年仅培养约5000名临床心理学专业毕业生——政府启动了一项加速培训计划，目标是通过高校扩招、在线认证和对现有医务人员的再培训，在三年内再培养3万名心理健康工作者。\n\n体重管理构成第二大支柱。鉴于肥胖和超重目前影响着超过50%的中国成年人——这一数字自2000年以来几乎翻了一番——该行动规定，所有社区卫生服务中心都必须提供免费营养咨询、运动处方和BMI筛查。一个显著特点是体重管理与心理健康服务的融合，这反映了越来越多的证据表明肥胖与抑郁是双向风险因素：两者都会增加对方发生的可能性，只治其一而不顾另一往往效果不佳。\n\n妇女健康受到特别关注。此前仅在部分城市面向13至15岁女孩开展的HPV疫苗接种项目，已扩展到全国范围，覆盖所有9至26岁的女孩和年轻女性，疫苗免费提供。此外，15个试点城市开始向同年龄段的男孩和年轻男性提供免费HPV疫苗接种，这体现了无性别差异接种在实现宫颈癌及其他HPV相关疾病群体免疫方面的作用。到2026年6月，扩大后的项目已接种超过1800万剂。\n\n癌症筛查也得到显著扩大。在成功试点项目的基础上，免费筛查针对……"
