            "answer": "B",
            "explanation": "细节理解题。问题问：哪个体育场将举办世界杯的开幕赛？根据原文 “The opening match will be held at Mexico City's iconic Estadio Azteca” (开幕赛将在墨西哥城标志性的阿兹特克体育场举 行)，可知B项正确。",
            "transcript": "The 2026 FIFA World Cup, scheduled from June 11 to July 19, will mark a historic first: for the first time in the tournament's 96-year history, the event will be hosted by three nations — the United States, Canada, and Mexico — spanning an entire continent.\n\nThe tournament will also be the first to feature 48 teams, expanding from the traditional 32-team format that had been in place since 1998. This expansion increases the total number of matches from 64 to 104, with the group stage consisting of 16 groups of three teams each. The top two teams from each group will advance to a new round of 32, followed by a knockout format familiar to fans worldwide.\n\nSixteen host cities have been selected: 11 in the United States (including New York/New Jersey, Los Angeles, Dallas, and Atlanta), 3 in Mexico (Mexico City, Monterrey, and Guadalajara), and 2 in Canada (Toronto and Vancouver). The opening match will be held at Mexico City's iconic Estadio Azteca, which will become the first stadium to host World Cup matches in three different tournaments (1970, 1986, and 2026). The final is scheduled for MetLife Stadium in East Rutherford, New Jersey.\n\nOrganizers estimate that over 5.5 million tickets will be sold, shattering previous records. The economic impact across the three host nations is projected to exceed $11 billion, with the creation of approximately 140,000 jobs. FIFA has also emphasized sustainability, pledging to offset all carbon emissions associated with the tournament and requiring all stadiums to meet stringent environmental standards.\n\nQuestion 9: How many teams will participate in the 2026 FIFA World Cup?\nQuestion 10: Which stadium will host the opening match of the tournament?\nQuestion 11: According to the passage, what is special about Estadio Azteca?",
            "translation": "2026年国际足联世界杯定于6月11日至7月19日举行，将创造历史性第一：在这项赛事96年的历史上，首次由三个国家——美国、加拿大和墨西哥——共同主办，横跨整个大洲。\n\n本届赛事也将是首届有48支球队参赛的世界杯，从自1998年以来一直沿用的32队赛制扩军而来。这一扩军使比赛总数从64场增加到104场，小组赛阶段由16个小组、每组3支球队组成。每组前两名将晋级全新的32强赛，之后进入全球球迷熟悉的淘汰赛制。\n\n共选定了16个主办城市：美国11个（包括纽约/新泽西、洛杉矶、达拉斯和亚特兰大），墨西哥3个（墨西哥城、蒙特雷和瓜达拉哈拉），加拿大2个（多伦多和温哥华）。揭幕战将在墨西哥城标志性的阿兹特克体育场举行，该体育场将成为首个在三届不同赛事（1970年、1986年和2026年）中承办世界杯比赛的球场。决赛定在新泽西州东卢瑟福的大都会人寿体育场举行。\n\n主办方估计将售出超过550万张门票，刷新历史纪录。三个主办国的经济影响预计将超过110亿美元，并创造约14万个就业岗位。国际足联还强调了可持续性，承诺抵消与赛事相关的所有碳排放，并要求所有场馆达到严格的环境标准。\n\nQuestion 9: 2026年国际足联世界杯将有多少支球队参赛？\nQuestion 10: 哪个体育场将承办本届赛事的揭幕战？\nQuestion 11: 根据短文，阿兹特克体育场有什么特别之处？"
