      "sampleEssay": "Combating Counterfeit Products: A Shared Responsibility\n\nThe proliferation of counterfeit products in mainstream supermarkets is a serious threat to consumer safety and market integrity. To protect consumers, a multi-pronged approach is necessary.\n\nFirst, governments must strengthen legal frameworks. This includes imposing stricter penalties on manufacturers and distributors of fakes, and establishing a more efficient system for product verification and traceability. Second, consumers should be educated to identify genuine products, report suspicious items, and prioritize authorized retailers. Third, supermarkets bear a crucial responsibility. As the final point of sale, they must implement rigorous supplier audits and random product inspections. They should not hide behind claims of ignorance; their duty of care to their customers requires them to be proactive in ensuring the authenticity of everything on their shelves. When a counterfeit is found, supermarkets should not only remove it immediately but also compensate affected consumers and publicly disclose the breach.\n\nIn conclusion, protecting consumers from counterfeit goods is a shared duty. While governments set the rules and consumers stay vigilant, supermarkets must act as the frontline guardians of trust. Their responsibility is absolute: to guarantee that the products they sell are safe and genuine.",
      "sampleEssayZh": "打击假冒伪劣产品：共同的责任\n\n假冒伪劣产品在主流超市中的泛滥，严重威胁着消费者安全和市场诚信。为了保护消费者，有必要采取多管齐下的方法。\n\n第一，政府必须加强法律框架。这包括对假冒产品的生产者和销售者施加更严厉的处罚，并建立更高效的产品验证与追溯体系。第二，应教育消费者学会识别正品、举报可疑商品，并优先选择正规授权的零售商。第三，超市肩负着至关重要的责任。作为销售的最后一环，它们必须实施严格的供应商审核和随机产品抽查。它们不应以不知情为借口推卸责任；对顾客的注意义务要求它们主动确保货架上所有商品均为正品。一旦发现假冒产品，超市不仅应立即下架，还应赔偿受影响的消费者，并公开披露这一违规行为。\n\n总之，保护消费者免受假冒商品之害是共同的责任。在政府制定规则、消费者保持警惕的同时，超市必须充当信任的前线守护者。它们的责任是绝对的：确保所售商品安全、正宗。"
