          "answer": "B",
          "explanation": "主旨大意题。问题问：这篇文章主要讲了什么？根据听力原文 \"if you know what to look for, you can use your own senses to make weather predictions\" (如果你知道观察什么，你可以用自己的感官来预测天气)，可知B项正确。",
          "transcript": "To find out what the weather is going to be, most people go straight to the radio, television, or newspaper to get an expert weather forecast. But if you know what to look for, you can use your own senses to make weather predictions. There are many signs that can help you. For example, in fair weather the air pressure is generally high, the air is still and often full of dust, and far away objects may look vague. But when a storm is brewing, the pressure drops, and you are often able to see things more clearly. Sailors took note of this long ago, and came up with the saying, \"The farther the sight, the nearer the rain.\" Your sense of smell can also help you detect weather changes. Just before it rains, odors become stronger. This is because odors are repressed in a fair high pressure center. When a bad weather low moves in, air pressure lessens and odors are released. You can also hear an approaching storm. Sounds bounce off heavy storm clouds and return to earth with increased force. An old saying describes it this way, \"Sounds traveling far and wide a stormy day will betide.\" And don't laugh at your grandmother if she says she can feel a storm coming. It is commonly known that many people feel pains in their bones or joints when the humidity rises, the pressure drops, and bad weather is on the way.",
          "translation": "为了知道天气会怎样，大多数人会直接打开收音机、电视或报纸，获取专家的天气预报。但如果你知道该观察什么，你也可以用自己的感官来预测天气。有许多迹象可以帮助你。例如，天气晴朗时气压通常较高，空气静止，常常充满灰尘，远处的物体可能显得模糊。但当暴风雨正在酝酿时，气压下降，你常常能更清楚地看到东西。水手们很久以前就注意到了这一点，并总结出这样的说法：“望得越远，雨越近。”你的嗅觉也能帮助你察觉天气变化。就在下雨前，气味会变得更浓。这是因为在晴朗的高压中心，气味受到抑制。当坏天气的低压移入时，气压降低，气味就释放出来。你还能听到暴风雨的临近。声音从厚重的暴风云上反弹回来，以更强的力量返回地面。有句老话这样描述：“声音传得又远又广，暴风雨的日子就要来临。”如果你的祖母说她能感觉到暴风雨要来，不要嘲笑她。众所周知，当湿度升高、气压下降、坏天气来临时，许多人会感到骨头或关节疼痛。"
