          "transcript": "M: I see from your resume that you worked as a manager of a store called Computer Country. Could you tell me a little more about your responsibilities there?\nW: Sure. I was responsible for overseeing about 30 employees. I did all of the orderings for the store and I kept track of the inventory.\nM: What was the most difficult part of your job?\nW: Probably handling angry customers. We didn't have them very often, but when we did, I needed to make sure they were well taken care of. After all, the customer is always right.\nM: That's how we feel here, too. How long did you work there?\nW: I was there for three and a half years. I left the company last month.\nM: And why did you leave?\nW: My husband has been transferred to Boston and I understand that your company has an opening there, too.\nM: Yes, that's right. We do. But the position won't start until early next month. Would that be a problem for you?\nW: No, not at all. My husband's new job doesn't begin for a few weeks, so we thought we would spend some time driving to Boston and stop to see my parents.\nM: That sounds nice. So, tell me, why are you interested in this particular position?\nW: I know that your company has a great reputation and wonderful product. I've thought many times that I would like to be a part of it. When I heard about the opening in Boston, I jumped at the opportunity.\nM: Well, I'm glad you did.\nQuestions 19 to 22 are based on the conversation you've just heard.\n19. What was the woman's previous job?\n20. What does the woman say was the most difficult part of her job?\n21. Why is the woman looking for a job in Boston?\n22. When can the woman start to work if she gets the job?",
          "translation": "男：我从你的简历上看到，你曾在一家叫“电脑王国”的商店担任经理。你能再详细说说你在那里的职责吗？\n女：当然。我负责管理大约30名员工。我负责店里所有的订货，并跟踪库存。\n男：你工作中最困难的部分是什么？\n女：大概是应付生气的顾客。我们并不经常遇到，但一旦遇到，我就得确保他们得到妥善照顾。毕竟，顾客永远是对的。\n男：我们这里也是这么认为的。你在那儿工作了多久？\n女：我在那里工作了三年半。我上个月离开了那家公司。\n男：你为什么离开呢？\n女：我丈夫被调到波士顿去了，我了解到贵公司在那边也有一个职位空缺。\n男：是的，没错。我们确实有。但这个职位要到下个月初才开始。这对你来说会有问题吗？\n女：不，完全没有问题。我丈夫的新工作几周后才开始，所以我们想花点时间开车去波士顿，顺便去看看我父母。\n男：听起来不错。那么，告诉我，你为什么对这个职位感兴趣？\n女：我知道贵公司声誉很好，产品也很出色。我很多次想过希望成为其中一员。当我听说波士顿有这个职位空缺时，我立刻抓住了这个机会。\n男：嗯，我很高兴你来了。\n第19至22题基于你刚才听到的对话。\n19. 女士之前的工作是什么？\n20. 女士说她的工作中最困难的部分是什么？\n21. 女士为什么在波士顿找工作？\n22. 如果女士得到这份工作，她什么时候可以开始工作？"
