          "answer": "C",
          "explanation": "细节理解题。问题问：胡安·路易斯从对听众的分析中了解到了什么？根据听力原文 \"only 2 or 3 of his classmates knew much of anything about geology\" (他的同学中只有两三个人对地质学有所了解)，可知C项正确。",
          "transcript": "Juan Louis, a junior geology major, decided to give an informative speech about how earthquakes occur. From his audience analysis he learned that only 2 or 3 of his classmates knew much of anything about geology. Juan realized then that he must present his speech at an elementary level and with a minimum of scientific language.\n\nAs he prepared the speech, Juan kept asking himself, \"How can I make this clear and meaningful to someone who knows nothing about earthquakes or geological principles?\" Since he was speaking in the Midwest, he decided to begin by noting that the most severe earthquake in American history took place not in California or Alaska but at New Madrid, Missouri in 1811. If such an earthquake happened today, it would be felt from the Rocky Mountains to the Atlantic Ocean and would flatten most of the cities in the Mississippi valley. That, he figured, should get his classmates' attention.\n\nThroughout the body of the speech, Juan dealt only with the basic mechanics of earthquakes and carefully avoided technical terms. He also prepared visual aids, diagramming fold lines, so his classmates wouldn't get confused. To be absolutely safe, Juan asked his roommate, who was not a geology major, to listen to the speech. \"Stop me,\" he said, \"any time I say something you don't understand.\" Juan's roommate stopped him four times. And at each spot, Juan worked out a way to make his point more clearly. Finally, he had a speech that was interesting and perfectly understandable to his audience.",
          "translation": "地质学专业大三学生胡安·路易斯决定做一场关于地震是如何发生的知识性演讲。通过听众分析，他了解到班上只有两三个同学对地质学有所了解。于是胡安意识到，他必须以基础的水平、尽量少用科学语言来呈现这场演讲。\n\n在准备演讲时，胡安不断地问自己：“我怎样才能让一个对地震或地质学原理一无所知的人听得明白、觉得有意义呢？”由于他是在中西部演讲，他决定开场先指出，美国历史上最严重的地震并不是发生在加利福尼亚或阿拉斯加，而是1811年发生在密苏里州的新马德里。如果今天发生这样一场地震，从落基山脉到大西洋都能感受到震感，密西西比河谷的大多数城市都会被夷为平地。他想，这样应该能吸引同学们的注意力。\n\n在演讲的主体部分，胡安只讲地震的基本原理，并小心地避开专业术语。他还准备了直观教具，画出褶皱线的图解，以免同学们感到困惑。为了绝对保险，胡安请一位非地质学专业的室友来听演讲。“只要我说了什么你不明白的，”他说，“就打断我。”室友打断了他四次。每次他都在那个地方想出一个办法，把观点讲得更清楚。最后，他完成了一场既有趣又能让听众完全听懂的演讲。"
