          "transcript": "W: You know I've often wondered why people laugh at the picture of a big belly businessman slipping on a banana skin and falling on his bottom. We are supposed to feel sorry for them.\nM: Actually, Laura, I think we laugh because we are glad it didn't happen to us. But of course there is also a kind of humorous satisfaction in seeing somebody self-important making a fool of themselves.\nW: Yes, and there are a lot of jokes about people who are too fat or physically handicapped, you know, deaf, or short-sighted things like that. After all, it's not really funny to be like that.\nM: Oh, I think that's because we're embarrassed. We don't know how to cope with the situation. Perhaps we are even a bit frightened we may get like that, so we laugh.\nW: What about the custard pie routine?\nM: What do you mean 'custard pie routine'?\nW: You know, all those old films where someone gets so outraged with his boss, he picks up a custard pie and plasters it all over the other person's face.\nM: That never makes me laugh much, because you can guess what's going to happen. But a lot of people still find it laughable. It must be because it's the sort of thing we'd all love to do once in a while and never quite have the courage to.\nW: I had an old aunt who used to throw cups of tea at people when she was particularly irritated. She said it relieved her feelings.\nM: It must have been a bit expensive.\nW: Not really. She took care never to throw her best china.\nQuestions 19 to 22 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n19.\tWhy does the man say we laugh when we see some self-important people making fools of themselves?\n20.\tWhy do some people joke about those who are fat or handicapped according to the man?\n21.\tWhy do many people find it funny to see someone throwing a custard pie on their boss's face?\n22.\tWhy does the man's aunt throw cups of tea at people occasionally?",
          "translation": "W: 你知道，我常常纳闷，为什么人们看到一个大腹便便的商人踩到香蕉皮摔个屁股蹲儿会发笑。我们本该同情他们才对。\nM: 其实，劳拉，我觉得我们笑是因为庆幸这没发生在自己身上。当然，看到那些自以为是的人出洋相，也会有一种滑稽的满足感。\nW: 是的，还有很多关于太胖或身体有缺陷的人的笑话，比如聋子、近视眼之类的。说到底，成为那样并不是什么好笑的事。\nM: 哦，我觉得那是因为我们感到尴尬。我们不知道该怎么应对那种情况。也许我们甚至有点害怕自己也会变成那样，所以才笑。\nW: 那扔奶油派的老套路呢？\nM: 你说的“扔奶油派的老套路”是什么意思？\nW: 你知道的，就是那些老电影里的情节——某个人被老板气坏了，就拿起一个奶油派糊到对方脸上。\nM: 那从来都不怎么让我发笑，因为你能猜到接下来会发生什么。但很多人还是觉得好笑。这一定是因为那是我们大家都偶尔想做、却又从来鼓不起勇气去做的事。\nW: 我以前有个老姑妈，特别生气的时候会把茶杯里的茶水泼向别人。她说这样能让她解气。\nM: 那一定有点费钱吧。\nW: 也不尽然。她很小心，从来不扔她最好的瓷器。\n\n第19至22题是根据你刚才听到的对话提出的。\n19. 男士为什么说，我们看到某些自以为是的人出洋相时会发笑？\n20. 根据男士的说法，为什么有些人会拿胖人或残疾人开玩笑？\n21. 为什么许多人觉得看到有人往老板脸上扔奶油派很好笑？\n22. 男士的姑妈为什么偶尔会向别人泼茶水？"
