          "answer": "C",
          "explanation": "原因目的题。问题问：说话人那天早上为什么自己修剪草坪？根据听力原文 \"That's a ridiculous stereotype. I'll show you who can do the best job on the lawn\" (那是荒谬的刻板印象，我要让你看看谁能把草坪打理得最好)，可知C项正确。",
          "transcript": "Somehow the old male and female stereotypes no longer fit. Men and women in this country haven't been fulfilling their traditional roles for some time now. And there seem to be fewer and fewer differences between the sexes. For instance, even though more women than men are still homemakers without paying jobs, women have been taking over more responsibility in the business world, earning higher salaries than ever before and entering fields of work that used to be exclusively male areas. At office meetings and in group discussions, they might speak up more often, express strong opinions and come up with more creative and practical ideas than their male colleagues. Several days ago, my 23-year-old daughter came to me with some important news. Not only had she found the highest paying job of her career, but she'd also accepted a date with the most charming man she'd ever met.\n\n\"Really?\" I responded, \"tell me about them.\"\n\n\"Receptionist in an attorney's office and a welder at a construction site.\" She answered in a matter-of-fact way. The interesting thing is my daughter's date is the receptionist and my daughter is the welder. The old stereotypes of men's and women's work have been changing more quickly than ever before, except perhaps in my own home.\n\n\"Who's going to mow the lawn?\" I asked my husband this morning.\n\n\"Oh, I will,\" he answered politely. \"That's men's work.\"\n\n\"What?\" Irritated, I raised my voice. \"That's a ridiculous stereotype. I'll show you who can do the best job on the lawn.\"\n\nThe work took 3 hours and I did it all myself.",
          "translation": "不知怎的，关于男性和女性的老一套刻板印象已不再适用了。在这个国家，男人和女人已经有一段时间不再扮演各自传统角色了，两性之间的差异似乎也越来越少。例如，尽管没有薪水、在家操持家务的女性仍多于男性，但女性已在商界承担起更多的责任，赚取比以往更高的薪水，并进入过去完全由男性占据的工作领域。在办公室会议和小组讨论中，她们可能更常发言，表达鲜明的观点，提出比男同事更有创意、更实用的想法。几天前，我23岁的女儿带来一个重要消息：她不仅找到了职业生涯中薪水最高的工作，还接受了和她所见过的最有魅力的男人的一次约会。\n\n“真的吗？”我回应道，“跟我说说他们。”\n\n“一个是律师事务所的前台接待，一个是建筑工地的焊工。”她以一种平淡的口吻回答。有意思的是，我女儿的约会对象是那位前台接待，而我女儿是那位焊工。关于男女工作的旧刻板印象正以前所未有的速度改变，只是在我自己家里可能除外。\n\n“谁来修剪草坪？”今天早上我问丈夫。\n\n“哦，我来吧，”他礼貌地回答，“那是男人的活儿。”\n\n“什么？”我生气地提高了嗓门，“那是个可笑的刻板印象。我要让你看看，谁修剪草坪最拿手。”\n\n这活儿花了3个小时，我全是一个人干完的。"
