          "transcript": "W: Oh, hello John. Are you using your dictating machine this morning? I've got a long report I must dictate. Can I borrow your machine?\nM: Of course. But can you spare me a second? It's the message you sent me about the delivery delay on the control desks. What's gone wrong?\nW: Everything, John. We have to get the steel sheets we need for these desks from new suppliers. Well, the suppliers have got some trouble or other. They say they will be a bit late for delivery.\nM: But they can't be. Those control desks are a special order. They are wanted for one of the big computer companies. It's a very important contract.\nW: When did we promise delivery?\nM: On Thursday next week. And there's a penalty clause. We stand to lose 10 percent of our price for each week of overdue delivery.\nW: Oh, these penalty clauses. Why do you sales people accept them?\nM: We have to accept them; otherwise, we don't get the contract.\nW: Well, let's get on to the Buying Department. I only heard about the delay yesterday because we kept the production line clear to handle the special sheets. It's a dreadful nuisance.\nM: It will be more than a nuisance if we don't meet the delivery date. It will cost us a lot of money.\nW: Keep calm, John. We can perhaps claim compensation from the steel suppliers for failure to deliver on time. That will offset the penalty clauses.\nM: Well, if you can.\nQuestions 9 to 12 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n9.\tWhy did the woman send the message to the man?\n10.\tWhat does the woman say about the new suppliers?\n11.\tHow did the man get the contract?\n12.\tWhat does the woman suggest they do?",
          "translation": "W: 哦，你好，约翰。你今天早上要用你的口述录音机吗？我有一份很长的报告要口述。能借用一下你的机器吗？\nM: 当然可以。不过你能给我一点时间吗？是你给我发的那条关于控制台交货延迟的消息。出了什么问题？\nW: 什么都出问题了，约翰。我们必须从新的供应商那里采购制作这些控制台所需的钢板。结果这些供应商遇到了这样那样的麻烦。他们说交货会晚一点。\nM: 但他们不能晚。那些控制台是特制订单，是给一家大型电脑公司定做的。这是一份非常重要的合同。\nW: 我们承诺什么时候交货？\nM: 下周四。而且还有违约金条款。每逾期交货一周，我们就要损失价格的10%。\nW: 哦，这些违约金条款。你们销售人员为什么要接受这些条款？\nM: 我们必须接受，否则就拿不到合同。\nW: 那咱们联系采购部吧。我昨天才听说延迟的事，因为我们一直把生产线空着来处理这些特制钢板。这真是件烦人的事。\nM: 如果我们不能按期交货，那可就不只是烦人了。会让我们损失很多钱。\nW: 冷静点，约翰。也许我们可以向钢铁供应商索要未按时交货的赔偿。那样就能抵消违约金条款了。\nM: 嗯，如果你能办到的话。\nQuestions 9 to 12 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n9.\t这位女士为什么给男士发消息？\n10.\t关于新的供应商，这位女士说了什么？\n11.\t男士是怎样拿到这份合同的？\n12.\t这位女士建议他们做什么？"
