          "answer": "D",
          "explanation": "细节理解题。问题问：女士说了她学校里女生的什么情况？根据听力原文 \"they have more opportunities to take the leading role in discussions and managerial responsibilities\" (她们有更多机会在讨论和管理职责中担任领导角色)，可知她们有更多机会培养领导能力，D项正确。",
          "transcript": "M: You are the headmistress of the Oxford High School for Girls. How many girls do you have here?\nW: We have 650 girls.\nM: In your experience, do girls do better academically and later professionally in single sex schools?\nW: Yes, I think they do better academically. And you can measure that very crudely from the examination results. I also think they do better academically because they have more opportunities to take the leading role in discussions and managerial responsibilities. I think they see the role models of chief positions of the school being held by women.\nM: I wonder if you could say then in a few words what the advantages are for a girl in the single sex school.\nW: Well, I think within the classroom, she is going to have full opportunity to express her own opinions. She isn't going to be shouted down by overconfident young gentlemen.\nM: Are teenagers in particular, do you think, shut out too much from the contact with the opposite sex? Does this cause difficulties when they find themselves in mixed groups?\nW: Well, I would like to find the parents who could shelter girls from the opposite sex if they live in Oxford. They encounter boys all the time socially out of school and through debating societies and things like that, some school activities as well.\nM: So, no disadvantages at all?\nW: I don't think there are any disadvantages. I think that it is grossly overstated that one needs to have contact with the opposite sex right through the whole of life in the classroom and outside the classroom at all ages.\nQuestions 13 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n13.\tWhat does the woman say about the girls in her school?\n14.\tWhat do we learn about the woman's school?\n15.\tWhat does the woman say about the girls' social life?",
          "translation": "M: 您是牛津女子高中的校长。你们学校有多少女生？\nW: 我们有650名女生。\nM: 以您的经验来看，女生在单性别学校里，学业表现以及日后的职业发展会更好吗？\nW: 是的，我认为她们在学业上表现更好。这一点你可以从考试成绩中非常粗略地衡量出来。我还认为她们在学业上表现更好，是因为她们有更多机会在讨论中担任主导角色，并承担管理职责。我觉得她们看到学校主要职位的榜样都由女性担任。\nM: 我想知道，您能否用几句话说说，对女生来说，在单性别学校就读有什么优势？\nW: 嗯，我认为在课堂上，她将有充分的机会表达自己的观点。她不会被过度自信的年轻男士们大声压下去。\nM: 您是否认为，尤其是青少年，被过多地隔绝了与异性的接触？当他们进入混合群体时，这会不会造成困难？\nW: 嗯，我倒想找找看，住在牛津的家长们有谁能让自己的女儿完全不接触异性。她们在校外的社交中，以及通过辩论社团之类的活动，还有一些学校活动中，一直都在接触男生。\nM: 那么，完全没有不利之处吗？\nW: 我认为没有任何不利之处。我认为，说什么人在一生中、在各个年龄段，都需要在课堂内外一直与异性接触，这种说法被严重夸大了。\nQuestions 13 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n13.\t关于她学校的女生，这位女士说了什么？\n14.\t关于这位女士的学校，我们能了解到什么？\n15.\t关于女生们的社交生活，这位女士说了什么？"
