          "transcript": "Karen Smith is a buyer for a department store in New York. Department store buyers purchase the goods that their stores sell. They not only have to know what is fashionable at the moment, but also have to guess what will become fashionable next season or next year. Most buyers work for just one department in a store. But the goods that Karen finds may be displayed and sold in several different sections of the store. Her job involves buying handicrafts from all over the world. Last year, she made a trip to Morocco and returned with rugs, pots, dishes and pans. The year before, she visited Mexico and bought back hand-made table cloths, mirrors with frames of tin and paper flowers. The paper flowers are bright and colorful, so they were used to decorate the whole store. This year Karen is travelling in Malaysia, Thailand and Indonesia. Many of the countries that Karen visits have government offices that promote handicrafts. The officials are glad to cooperate with her by showing her the products that are available. Karen especially likes to visit markets in small towns and villages whenever she can arrange for it. She is always looking for interesting and unusual items. Karen thinks she has the best job she could have found. She loves all the travelling that she has to do because she often visits markets and small out-of-the-way places. She sees much more of the country she visits than an ordinary tourist would. As soon as she gets back to New York from one trip, Karen begins to plan another.",
          "translation": "卡伦·史密斯是纽约一家百货商店的采购员。百货商店的采购员负责采购店里销售的商品。他们不仅要知道当下流行什么，还要猜测下一季或明年会流行什么。大多数采购员只为店里的一个部门工作，但卡伦找到的商品可能会在店里好几个不同的区域陈列和销售。她的工作包括从世界各地采购手工艺品。去年，她去了一趟摩洛哥，带回了地毯、陶罐、盘碟和平底锅。前一年，她去了墨西哥，买回了手工桌布、锡框镜子和纸花。这些纸花鲜艳多彩，所以被用来装饰整个商店。今年，卡伦正在马来西亚、泰国和印度尼西亚旅行。卡伦到访的许多国家都有推广手工艺品的政府机构，官员们很乐意与她合作，向她展示可提供的产品。只要有机会，卡伦特别喜欢逛小城镇和村庄的市场。她总是在寻找有趣而不同寻常的物品。卡伦觉得自己找到了能找到的最好的工作。她热爱所有必须进行的旅行，因为她经常逛市场和偏僻的小地方。她看到的所访国家的面貌，比普通游客要多得多。每次旅行一回到纽约，卡伦就开始计划下一次旅行。"
