          "answer": "A",
          "explanation": "细节理解题。问题问：男士说大多数人陷入恋爱关系时是怎样的？根据听力原文 \"People often get into love affairs because they have unrealistic expectations about somebody.\" (人们陷入恋爱关系往往是因为对对方抱有不切实际的期望)，可知A项正确。",
          "transcript": "W: Charles, among other things, you are regarded as one of America's great masters of the Blues — a musical idiom that is essentially about loss, particularly the loss of romantic love. Why does love die?\nM: People often get into love affairs because they have unrealistic expectations about somebody. Then when the person doesn't turn out to be who they thought he or she was, they start thinking \"maybe I can change him or her.\" That kind of thinking is a mistake. Because when the dust settles, people are going to be pretty much what they are. It's a rare thing for anybody to be able to change who they really are. And this creates a lot of problems.\nW: At 62, you continue to spend a large percentage of your life touring. What appeals to you about life on the road?\nM: Music. I don't especially love life on the road, but I figure if you are lucky enough to be able to do what you truly love doing, you've got the ultimate in life.\nW: What's the most widely-held misconception about the life of a famous musician?\nM: People think it's all glamour. Actually we have the same troubles as they do. Playing music doesn't mean life treats you any better.\nW: How do you feel about being recognized everywhere you go?\nM: You'd think I'd be used to it by now. But I still find it fascinating. You go to a little town in Japan, where nobody speaks English, yet they know you on sight and know all your music. I'm still amazed by the love people express for me and for my music.\n12. What does the man say about most people when they get into love affairs?\n13. What does the man say about himself as a singer on the road most of his life?\n14. What do most people think of the life of a famous musician?\n15. How does the man feel whenever he is recognized by his fans?",
          "translation": "W: 查尔斯，除了其他成就之外，你被认为是美国最伟大的布鲁斯音乐大师之一——布鲁斯是一种本质上关于失去、尤其是失去浪漫爱情的音乐风格。爱情为什么会消逝？\nM: 人们之所以常常陷入恋爱，是因为他们对某个人抱有不切实际的期望。然后，当那个人并不是他们想象中的样子时，他们就开始想“也许我能改变他或她”。这种想法是错误的。因为当尘埃落定，人基本上还是原来的样子。任何人能改变自己真实本性的情况都极为罕见。而这会造成很多问题。\nW: 62岁了，你仍然把生活中的很大一部分时间花在巡回演出上。路上的生活有什么吸引你的地方？\nM: 音乐。我并不特别喜欢路上的生活，但我想，如果你足够幸运，能做自己真正热爱的事情，你就拥有了生活中最极致的东西。\nW: 关于著名音乐家的生活，最普遍存在的误解是什么？\nM: 人们以为那全是光鲜亮丽。实际上，我们和他们一样有同样的烦恼。演奏音乐并不意味着生活会对你更好。\nW: 无论走到哪里都被人认出来，你感觉如何？\nM: 你会以为我到现在已经习惯了。但我仍然觉得这很奇妙。你去日本的一个小镇，那里没人会说英语，但他们一眼就认出你，还知道你所有的音乐。人们对我以及我的音乐所表达的爱，至今仍让我感到惊讶。\n\n12. 关于大多数人陷入恋爱时的情况，男士说了什么？\n13. 关于自己大半生在路上巡演的歌手的身份，男士说了什么？\n14. 大多数人认为著名音乐家的生活是怎样的？\n15. 每当被歌迷认出来时，男士感觉如何？"
